label beginbinarylevel (startbinarylevel)
"Mystery Guide": This is trail of binary system
"Mystery Guide": As the name suggests, the binary system means there are only two possible values
0 and 1.
"Mystery Guide": Let’s go check what you have to do in this trail”
jump describemechanic
[end_timeline]


label describemechanic (describemechanic)
"Mystery Guide": There is a random switch or *‘the Ancient Pulse’*
"Mystery Guide": It pulses with the will of a bygone age. Press — and let fate decide.
"Mystery Guide": You have to interact with it to determine the amount of power the trail requires each time.
"Mystery Guide": There are also have *‘The Sigil Array’*  that contain many *dual sigils*”
"Mystery Guide": Do not forget to *confirm* the values you’ve given.”
"Mystery Guide": Without it, the trail shall not know if your path was true.”
"Mystery Guide": Yet at times, it must first be activated by *‘The Awakener Sigil’* before it may receive your touch.”
jump understandmechanic
[end_timeline]


label understandmechanic (understandmechanic)
So… I have to press a random switch to see what the result will be
After that, I need to input the value on the panel based on the random number.
However, sometimes I have to activate the activation button first before doing that.
Am I right?
"Mystery Guide": Indeed, as I had imagined, you are sharp of mind.
"Mystery Guide": No matter how elegantly I weave my words, you grasp their meaning with ease.
"Mystery Guide": How truly impressive.
…
Thanks?


So, um… how does this thing—the Sigil Array—actually work?
jump describebinarypanel
[end_timeline]


label describebinarypanel (describebinarypanel)
"Mystery Guide": As I mentioned, each dual sigil have two values\: either 0 or 1
"Mystery Guide": When set in place—one after another—their order creates a new amount of power.
"Mystery Guide": Here, the flow of the power runs left to right… then top to bottom.
"Mystery Guide": Touch them, and you'll feel it—the sigil in the bottom-right is the lowest power.
"Mystery Guide": While the top-left contains the greatest power.
jump calculatebinary
[end_timeline]


label calculatebinary (calculatebinary)
"Mystery Guide": Begin with the base—two, for such is the rule of the Binary trail.
"Mystery Guide": Raise it high, to match the sigil’s position, then bind it with your chosen value—0 or 1.
"Mystery Guide": To understand the sigil’s position…”
"Mystery Guide": We start with the lowest power at the bottom-right, counting from 0, and rise to the greatest power at the top-left.
jump examplebinary
[end_timeline]


label examplebinary (examplebinary)
"Mystery Guide": For example… take the top-left sigil.
"Mystery Guide": Suppose you place a 1 within it—then it becomes 1 × 2⁷… which gives you 128.
"Mystery Guide": And if you place 1 to several sigils at once, their pulses will not stand alone.
"Mystery Guide": They will gather, add together, and form a single new power
jump concludemachanic
[end_timeline]


label concludemachanic (concludemachanic)
"Mystery Guide": Do you have any questions?
* How the overall system work
"Mystery Guide": ‘the Ancient Pulse’ use to random amount of power that you have to create”
"Mystery Guide": the Dual Sigil’ is use to input value either 0 or 1
"Mystery Guide": ‘the Sigil Array’ is the panel that contain many dual sigils
"Mystery Guide": ‘the Awakener Sigil’ use to activate some sigil array that have been deactivate
- How does the Sigil Array work?
	jump describebinarypanel
- How to calculate by using the Sigil Array?
	jump calculatebinary
