label beginoctallevel (startoctallevel)
"Mystery Guide": This is trail of octal system
White (ThinkWhite): Why doesn’t this place feel like a trail at all?
"Mystery Guide": This place is not merely an ancient trail. It has… threads from other realms woven into it.
"Mystery Guide": Artifacts and fragments from elsewhere sometimes slip through and find their way here.
"Mystery Guide": Go on—approach that cube.
jump describeoctalcube (describeoctalcube)
[end_timeline]


label describeoctalcube (describeoctalcube)
"Mystery Guide": This is a different kind of Sigil Array…* the Sigil Cube*.
"Mystery Guide": It is used to uncover values in the octal system.
"Mystery Guide": You see, three binary digits—three dual sigils—can be woven together to form values up to 8.
"Mystery Guide": So in truth, each octal digit is a blend… a harmony of three simple sigils.
"Mystery Guide": Touch it—and learn with your own hands.
[end_timeline]


